IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- SCHEDULE 5 -- CONNECTED PERSONS (S.I. 2017/692, lines 3242-3255 of the plain-text rendering,
-- which is not the official text and is not verified against it).
--
-- WHAT IT IS FOR.  Regulation 65(3) (encoded by part mlr4) says a person is a "connected person" of a
-- relevant person or payment service provider "if that person is a person listed in Schedule 5 in
-- relation to the relevant person or payment service provider"; a supervisory authority may then
-- require a connected person to give information by notice (reg 66(1), line 2217) and the relevant person and
-- any connected person must give a skilled person all reasonable assistance (line 2401).  This module is that Schedule: SEAM S-16, answered
-- here for part mlr4.
--
-- THE SUBJECT.  The Schedule speaks of "the relevant person or payment service provider" in every
-- paragraph; this module calls it "the subject" in comments and takes its legal form from the core's
-- `Form of customer` (the core's list is the same list of legal forms; it is used for the subject here,
-- not for a customer).  Whether the subject IS a relevant person or a payment service provider is the
-- caller's step (S-8 for a relevant person); it is not asked again here.
--
-- "OFFICER", "MANAGER" AND THE OTHER ROLES.  Regulation 3(1) defines "officer" "except in Part 8 and
-- Schedule 5" (line 88), so the defined meaning is switched off inside this Schedule: "officer" here is
-- an undefined term (FINDING 1 in NOTES.md).  Every role below is therefore a plain BOOLEAN fact that
-- a witness can state: "this person is, or at any time has been, an officer of the subject", and so on.
--
-- THE FORM OF THE SUBJECT (FORK S5-F1 in NOTES.md).  Paragraph 1 is "a body corporate", paragraph 2 "a
-- partnership", paragraph 3 "an unincorporated association of persons which is not a partnership",
-- paragraph 4 "an individual".  The core separates the forms.  Regulation 3(1) says "body corporate"
-- includes a body corporate incorporated under the laws of the United Kingdom or any part of it, or
-- constituted under the law of another country, and does not include a corporation sole or a partnership
-- that is not regarded as a body corporate under the law that governs it (lines 26-32).  So: a company and
-- `a body corporate of another kind` are the body corporate of paragraph 1; `a corporation sole` is not.
-- `a limited liability partnership` is placed in paragraph 1: the core lists it as a form of its own, the rendering of the definition does not name it, and a limited liability partnership
-- is taken to be a body corporate incorporated under the law of the United Kingdom (reading A, taken; reading B puts it in paragraph 2 as a partnership; this part is a judgement the
-- text does not make, so it is a fork, S5-F1, and a marginal reading for a lawyer).
-- `a partnership other than a limited liability partnership` is paragraph 2; `an unincorporated
-- association` is paragraph 3; `an individual` is paragraph 4.  A trust, a foundation, an estate and
-- `another legal entity or legal arrangement` are none of the four.

-- src:3242 | SCHEDULE 5 — Connected Persons
§ `Schedule 5 -- Connected Persons`

-- The roles a person has, or at any time has had, in relation to the subject.  Each is a fact; none is a
-- defined term of these Regulations in this Schedule (see the header).
DECLARE `sch 5 roles of the person` HAS
    `officer of the subject`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `manager of the subject`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `officer of a parent undertaking of the subject` IS A BOOLEAN
    `manager of a parent undertaking of the subject` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employee of the subject`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `agent of the subject`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `agent of a parent undertaking of the subject` IS A BOOLEAN
    `member of the subject`                        IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The four forms of the subject, in the core's words.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref sch 5 para 1 (the form of the subject, as the first words of the paragraph)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 1 the subject is a body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `a company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a body corporate of another kind` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref sch 5 para 2 (the form of the subject, as the first words of the paragraph)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 2 the subject is a partnership` MEANS
    form EQUALS `a partnership other than a limited liability partnership`

@ref sch 5 para 3 (the form of the subject, as the first words of the paragraph)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 3 the subject is an unincorporated association of persons which is not a partnership` MEANS
    form EQUALS `an unincorporated association`

@ref sch 5 para 4 (the form of the subject, as the first words of the paragraph)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 4 the subject is an individual` MEANS
    form EQUALS `an individual`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The four paragraphs.
--
-- Each answers JUST TRUE for a listed role; NOTHING when the paragraph applies to the subject and
-- the person has none of the listed roles (the paragraph lists persons and does not say "only", so
-- it does not say that anyone else is not connected: regulation 65(3) closes the list with "if", and
-- that is part mlr4's rule); JUST FALSE when the paragraph's own "If the relevant person ... is ..."
-- does not hold of the subject (Marginal readings, (a): a failed "if" counts as the text's no).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3243 | 1 Corporate Bodies
-- src:3244 | If the relevant person or payment service provider is a body corporate, any person who is or has been—
-- src:3245 | (a) an officer or manager of the body corporate;
-- src:3246 | (b) an officer or manager of a parent undertaking of the body corporate;
-- src:3247 | (c) an employee of the body corporate;
-- src:3248 | (d) an agent of the body corporate; or
-- src:3249 | (e) an agent of a parent undertaking of the body corporate.
@ref sch 5 para 1 (src:3243-3249)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
      roles IS A `sch 5 roles of the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 1 the person is a connected person of the body corporate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`sch 5 para 1 the subject is a body corporate` form)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the relevant person or payment service provider is a body corporate" fails; Marginal readings, (a)
        IF     roles's `officer of the subject`
            OR roles's `manager of the subject`
            OR roles's `officer of a parent undertaking of the subject`
            OR roles's `manager of a parent undertaking of the subject`
            OR roles's `employee of the subject`
            OR roles's `agent of the subject`
            OR roles's `agent of a parent undertaking of the subject`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists the persons who are connected and does not say that no one else is

-- src:3250 | 2 Partnerships
-- src:3251 | If the relevant person or payment service provider is a partnership, any person who is or has been a member, manager, employee or agent of the partnership.
@ref sch 5 para 2 (src:3250-3251)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
      roles IS A `sch 5 roles of the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 2 the person is a connected person of the partnership` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`sch 5 para 2 the subject is a partnership` form)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the relevant person or payment service provider is a partnership" fails; Marginal readings, (a)
        IF     roles's `member of the subject`
            OR roles's `manager of the subject`
            OR roles's `employee of the subject`
            OR roles's `agent of the subject`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists the persons who are connected and does not say that no one else is

-- src:3252 | 3 Unincorporated Associations
-- src:3253 | If the relevant person or payment service provider is an unincorporated association of persons which is not a partnership, any person who is or has been a member, an officer, manager, employee or agent of the association.
@ref sch 5 para 3 (src:3252-3253)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
      roles IS A `sch 5 roles of the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 3 the person is a connected person of the unincorporated association` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`sch 5 para 3 the subject is an unincorporated association of persons which is not a partnership` form)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the relevant person or payment service provider is an unincorporated association of persons which is not a partnership" fails; Marginal readings, (a)
        IF     roles's `member of the subject`
            OR roles's `officer of the subject`
            OR roles's `manager of the subject`
            OR roles's `employee of the subject`
            OR roles's `agent of the subject`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists the persons who are connected and does not say that no one else is

-- src:3254 | 4 Individuals
-- src:3255 | If the relevant person or payment service provider is an individual, any person who is or has been an employee or agent of that individual.
@ref sch 5 para 4 (src:3254-3255)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
      roles IS A `sch 5 roles of the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 4 the person is a connected person of the individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`sch 5 para 4 the subject is an individual` form)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the relevant person or payment service provider is an individual" fails; Marginal readings, (a)
        IF     roles's `employee of the subject`
            OR roles's `agent of the subject`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists the persons who are connected and does not say that no one else is

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B, as guidance for gathering a legal effect's routes by hand
-- only): the person is a connected person of the subject if any of the four paragraphs says so.
-- Every paragraph also has its own function above (option C).  No construct that gathers by name is used.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- SEAM S-16 (answering): part mlr4, reg 65(3), asks `sch 5 the person is a connected person of the
-- relevant person`; the merge replaces its input with a call to this function.
--
-- Regulation 65(3) (line 2215) says a person is connected to a relevant person or a payment service provider "if that person is a person listed in Schedule 5 in
-- relation to the relevant person or payment service provider": the definition of "a connected person" is handed to the Schedule's list.
-- By Meng's ruling of 2026-11-05 on a definition handed to a list, a person who is within no paragraph is not a connected person: JUST FALSE.
-- This function therefore answers JUST TRUE if any paragraph does, and otherwise JUST FALSE, whether the subject's form fits no paragraph (a trust, a
-- corporation sole) or the form fits a paragraph and the person has none of its roles.  Each paragraph's own function above still answers NOTHING for a person
-- with none of its roles, because a paragraph that lists persons without "only" does not by itself say that no one else is connected (Marginal readings, (b)); the no
-- comes from regulation 65(3).  All the facts are BOOLEANs and a form, so the answer is never unknown.
@ref sch 5 (paragraphs 1 to 4 together)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
      roles IS A `sch 5 roles of the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 the person is a connected person of the relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `sch 5 para 1 the person is a connected person of the body corporate` form roles EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `sch 5 para 2 the person is a connected person of the partnership` form roles EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `sch 5 para 3 the person is a connected person of the unincorporated association` form roles EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `sch 5 para 4 the person is a connected person of the individual` form roles EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 65(3), "a person is connected ... if that person is a person listed in Schedule 5", hands the definition to the Schedule's list, and the person is within no paragraph; Meng's ruling of 2026-11-05 on a definition handed to a list
